data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" garden is not a \"set it and forget it\" project; it is a living system that requires consistent care.\n\n","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"*   **Watering:** Aim for consistency. It is better to water deeply a few times a week than to give","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" a light sprinkle every day. This encourages roots to grow deeper into the soil. Always water at the base of the plant","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" to keep the leaves dry, which helps prevent fungal diseases.\n*   **Mulching:** Spread a layer of straw","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":", shredded leaves, or wood chips around your plants. Mulch acts like a blanket, keeping moisture in the soil and","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" suppressing weed growth.\n*   **Weeding:** Pull weeds as soon as you see them. Weeds compete with","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" your vegetables for nutrients and water, and if left unchecked, they can quickly overtake your garden.\n*   **P","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

